<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Damavand</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damavand">Damavand</a> is a dormant volcano in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a> range of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, about 5,610 metres high and the highest peak in Iran. It features widely in Persian myth and poetry: in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahnameh">Shahnameh</a> the tyrant Zahhak is chained in a cave on the mountain. Its slopes and valleys gave refuge to local dynasties such as the Masmughans, who ruled the district in the early Islamic period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-damavand.jpg" alt="Mount Damavand" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Safa.daneshvar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:981012-Damavand-South-IMG_9861-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
